## Summary

**What was failing and why:**

1. **Infinite loop on stdin**: The `read_line()` function would return an empty buffer (length 0) when EOF was reached after consuming all input, causing the main loop to continue indefinitely.

2. **`--` terminator not handled**: The code checked for unknown options before processing the `--` terminator, so arguments like `-alpha` after `--` were incorrectly rejected as unknown options.

**What I changed:**

1. Fixed `read_line()` at `/Users/sonjabrown/agentic_cyber/runs/formal/grep-qwen3-topk50-t0-p01-seed42-maxtok32768-loops3-n10/lineage-008/000/temp-0p0/attempt-001/workdir/src/new_grep/new_grep.c:18-27` to return NULL when EOF is reached with no data read (previously it would break and return an empty buffer).

2. Rewrote `main()` at `/Users/sonjabrown/agentic_cyber/runs/formal/grep-qwen3-topk50-t0-p01-seed42-maxtok32768-loops3-n10/lineage-008/000/temp-0p0/attempt-001/workdir/src/new_grep/new_grep.c:132-191` to:
   - First scan for `--` terminator
   - Set the pattern index based on where `--` is found (or default to 1)
   - Extract pattern from the correct position
   - Process files starting after the pattern

**Build command run:**
```
mkdir -p build && cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic -O2 src/new_grep/new_grep.c -o build/new_grep
```

**Which failing tests I expect to pass now:**
All 51 base tests should pass (previously only 10 passed, 41 were timing out or failing).
